{"kind":"report","text":"Changes requested for CLI JSON design exact65609bac7ed94112149c6f39cd7acba7f692dc97, primary notes/2026-10-12-cli-json-output-design.md.\n\n[P2] Make the envelope represent every workflow phase coherently (§5,7,12). result is restricted to done/partial but unsupported clone requires result.git; recorded excludes refused but late-refused merge requires it. Mandatory RefusalReason/judgedAt applies to native Answer.refused, not Founded.refused or a host mint/publication refusal after acceptance. Define phase-specific shapes retaining native answers, accepted facts and later observed facts; do not invent a judged head or discard acceptance. Preserve known receipts through later session/credential/Git failures. Move rate-limited to unavailable. The explicitly open inconsistent decision can retain exit1/result once normalized across the envelope and schema.\n\n[P2] Preserve current exit codes and flag-value ownership (§3,4,7). At immutable013fac, invite/verifyAll/issues return usage2 when no repository is configured, whereas the note calls those not-found1. Reconcile with flag-only unchanged exits. Parser values such as --title --json own the next token; global switch extraction must distinguish option positions from consumed data and test that case. Redirect every child Git run, including preflight, to stderr in JSON mode. Read-forbidden/unavailable is unreadable, not proof that a scope is absent.\n\n[P2] Correct issues aggregation and text parity (§7.20,8). Source issuesOf1693–1712 reads the directory index and each issue lane summary; lane closure can leave the index stale. Preserve each actual lane head/ScopeRef, closeReason, assignees array and nullable number. One directory head and one optional assignee cannot describe those reads or reproduce current text showing reasons/all assignees. Claim no cross-scope snapshot. Distinguish friendly command labels from native close-own/close-any kinds.\n\n[P2] State truthful read completeness and aggregate bounds (§7.9,9). The log input union drops native timed/diagnosis/preparation/outcome/checkpoint, which entryLine emits today. Native log exhausts1000 pages without checking completion; --limit only slices and has no absolute bound. verifyAll's1000-page bound is per discovered scope, not a global scope/byte bound. Specify reached-head versus exhausted/unreadable results with retained cursors and explicit aggregate budgets/continuations. Preserve valid data and full functionality; a single document remains possible without adding JSON-lines now.\n\n[P2] Define safe unexpected-error conversion (§5,11,12). Raw Error.message can contain forbidden config/private/key paths (files.ts45,68,75,83); a renderer without Context still leaks a copied message. Allowlist public codes/messages and use a fixed safe unknown-error value. Add path/credential-bearing exception witnesses. Deliberate invite output under confidential and native history remain explicit separate boundaries; native enrol history may retain supplied invitation secret. Git stderr is a trusted child boundary, not a document confidentiality guarantee.\n\nArchitecture: one typed result with two renderers is sound after coherent phase/provenance and read shapes. Security: private result construction must be enforced before rendering; unknown/no-answer must retain original-request recovery rather than license a fresh mutation. Simplification: one global option and one envelope are useful; remove contradictory special cases by schema variants, not lost evidence.\n\nSection13 preferences: retain inconsistent with exit1/result; defer full catalog/environment default/streaming flags with explicit ownership; keep confidential wrapper, done facts in result only, and publish schema in packages/cli/schema. These preferences grant no implementation authority. Entry.v exists: no finding there.\n\nValidation: primary37199B/706LF FULL Root and two peers; both finals/audits FULL Root. Native full selected files and every bounded partial command/contract fragment verified; no whole135560B commands.ts claim. Root audit389B SHA0ee9ce857c9b9db7b34aa256d86898709667d3eca207705adfe12457253913ef. No Source execution/tests/gate/install/provider/browser/private reads. Design-only assigned6a9/845 binding; no implementation/publication/deployment or before-demo work approved.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:f191f6d7900f09602dc9d456758803c3c83a4156","binding":"assigned","head":"65609bac7ed94112149c6f39cd7acba7f692dc97","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:5c7b55cca6e4497e2272d3c9536a1797df244370\",\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:5317f569654b2af10d77ce2bbe04cbcea86cdd87\"]","implementations":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:84506c10d8ccda1df931f6d1ebbbebc09061cc52\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:7fe21a4f895759a588cda5393db9c8c9a9b2495c","review_path":"reviewguard@1","verdict":"changes-requested"}}